   "updated": 1764150000000,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "How several projects share ONE database safely\n1. One Postgres, one schema per project + a shared core schema. A project writes only to its own schema.\n2. Shared data (customers, products, stock, orders) is written only through the Hub API, never by another app's SQL.\n3. Every record has one owner (system of record), see the table on the right.\n4. One hub ID per customer/product + external_ids map (ERP, HubSpot, Zendesk, Nuacom ids), so data is entered once.\n5. Every change writes an event to the outbox in the same transaction; workers deliver it (Teams, HubSpot, ERP). No app polls\n  another.\n6. A separate DB login per project with least privilege; reporting uses a read-only login on views.\n7. Versioned migrations per schema, in one repo, with docs, so knowledge isn't tied to one person.",
   "originalText": "How several projects share ONE database safely\n1. One Postgres, one schema per project + a shared core schema. A project writes only to its own schema.\n2. Shared data (customers, products, stock, orders) is written only through the Hub API, never by another app's SQL.\n3. Every record has one owner (system of record), see the table on the right.\n4. One hub ID per customer/product + external_ids map (ERP, HubSpot, Zendesk, Nuacom ids), so data is entered once.\n5. Every change writes an event to the outbox in the same transaction; workers deliver it (Teams, HubSpot, ERP). No app polls\n  another.\n6. A separate DB login per project with least privilege; reporting uses a read-only login on views.\n7. Versioned migrations per schema, in one repo, with docs, so knowledge isn't tied to one person.",
   "fontSize": 18,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": "r0315",
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "r0317",
